---
import Entry from '../../../layouts/Entry.astro';
import Faq from '../../../components/registry/Faq.astro';
import '../../../styles/registry-wave1.css';
import { absolute, url } from '../../../lib/site';
import { wave1, faqNode, hubNodes, count, dayLabel, usStatePath, US_BASE, EW_BASE, WAVE1_DATA_PATH } from '../../../lib/registry-wave1';
import { wave1b, sentence, SC_BASE, AU_BASE, CA_BASE, CAUSE_PATH, WAVE1B_DATA_PATH } from '../../../lib/registry-wave1b';

const w = wave1();
const b = wave1b();
const faqs = b.dossierIndexFaqs();
const canonical = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site).toString();
const origin = absolute('/', Astro.site);
const title = 'Verified charity dossiers';
const description = `${count(w.us.length + w.ew.length + b.sc.length + b.au.length + b.ca.length)} dossiers from five official registers: the United States, England and Wales, Scotland, Australia and Canada, with state, NTEE, purpose, subtype and category hubs. Figures as published, never rated.`;
const files = Object.values(w.manifest.outputs) as { path: string; bytes: number; sha256: string }[];
const filesB = Object.values(b.manifest.outputs) as { path: string; bytes: number; sha256: string }[];
const jsonLd = [
  ...hubNodes({
    name: title, description, canonical, origin,
    items: [
      { name: 'United States charity dossiers', url: absolute(US_BASE, Astro.site) },
      { name: 'England and Wales charity dossiers', url: absolute(EW_BASE, Astro.site) },
      { name: 'Scotland charity dossiers', url: absolute(SC_BASE, Astro.site) },
      { name: 'Australia charity dossiers', url: absolute(AU_BASE, Astro.site) },
      { name: 'Canada charity dossiers', url: absolute(CA_BASE, Astro.site) },
      { name: 'Cause × Country: charity dossiers by registry category', url: absolute(CAUSE_PATH, Astro.site) },
    ],
    spatialCoverage: 'United States; England and Wales; Scotland; Australia; Canada',
    dataFiles: [
      absolute(`${WAVE1_DATA_PATH}manifest.json`, Astro.site), ...files.map((f) => absolute(`${WAVE1_DATA_PATH}${f.path}`, Astro.site)),
      absolute(`${WAVE1B_DATA_PATH}manifest.json`, Astro.site), ...filesB.map((f) => absolute(`${WAVE1B_DATA_PATH}${f.path}`, Astro.site)),
    ],
    isBasedOn: [w.bmf.page, w.soi.page, w.register.page, b.src.oscrRegister.page, b.src.acncRegister.page, b.src.craIdentification['2024'].catalogue],
    license: 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/',
    creditText: 'Internal Revenue Service public records; Charity Commission for England and Wales and Office of the Scottish Charity Regulator information under the Open Government Licence v3.0; ACNC data under CC BY 3.0 AU; Canada Revenue Agency information under the Open Government Licence – Canada; selected and formatted by Charitology.',
  }),
  faqNode(faqs),
];
const sources = [
  { title: 'Exempt Organizations Business Master File Extract (EO BMF)', publisher: 'Internal Revenue Service', url: w.bmf.page },
  { title: 'Annual extract of tax-exempt organization financial data', publisher: 'Internal Revenue Service, Statistics of Income', url: w.soi.page },
  { title: 'Register of charities: full register download and data definitions', publisher: 'Charity Commission for England and Wales', url: w.register.page },
  { title: 'Download the Scottish Charity Register', publisher: 'Office of the Scottish Charity Regulator', url: b.src.oscrRegister.page },
  { title: 'Download Charity Register data', publisher: 'Australian Charities and Not-for-profits Commission', url: b.src.acncRegister.page },
  { title: '2024 List of charities', publisher: 'Canada Revenue Agency', url: b.src.craIdentification['2024'].catalogue },
  { title: 'Open Government Licence v3.0', publisher: 'The National Archives', url: w.register.licence },
];
---

<Entry
  title={title}
  eyebrow="The Record · Global Charity Index"
  summary="One page per organization, built only from official registry records and published financial figures, each with its source file, date, record number and fingerprint."
  description={description}
  crumbs={[{ label: 'The Record', href: '/record/' }, { label: 'Charity dossiers' }]}
  sources={sources}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  sections={[
    { slug: 'registers', text: 'Registers and thresholds', symbol: 'archive' },
    { slug: 'hubs', text: 'Browse the hubs', symbol: 'map' },
    { slug: 'files', text: 'Dataset files', symbol: 'download' },
    { slug: 'questions', text: 'Questions answered from the record', symbol: 'question' },
  ]}
>
  <p>A verified charity dossier reproduces what an official register publishes about one organization: its identifier, registry codes, classifications and financial figures, each cited to the exact source file and record. Charitology adds no rating, score, overhead ratio, estimate or effectiveness claim. Dossiers are listed alphabetically.</p>

  <h2 id="registers">Registers and thresholds</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data rw-table">
      <caption>Dossier coverage. Each threshold uses one published figure from the latest period, in the register’s own currency. Wave 1 covers the United States and England and Wales; Wave 1b adds Scotland, Australia and Canada.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Register</th><th scope="col">Inclusion threshold</th><th scope="col" class="num">Dossiers</th><th scope="col">Source dates</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href={url(US_BASE)}>United States</a><span class="rw-sub">IRS EO BMF and Form 990 extracts</span></th>
          <td>Total revenue of at least {w.usThreshold}</td>
          <td class="num">{count(w.us.length)}</td>
          <td>EO BMF last modified {w.bmfPosted}; Form 990 extracts for calendar years {w.extractYears(w.us).join(' and ')}</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href={url(EW_BASE)}>England and Wales</a><span class="rw-sub">Charity Commission register</span></th>
          <td>Gross income of at least {w.ewThreshold}</td>
          <td class="num">{count(w.ew.length)}</td>
          <td>Register extract dated {w.registerDate}; annual return edition of {dayLabel(w.manifest.sources.ccewAnnualReturns.edition)}</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href={url(SC_BASE)}>Scotland</a><span class="rw-sub">Scottish Charity Register (OSCR), Wave 1b</span></th>
          <td>Gross income of at least {b.scThreshold}</td>
          <td class="num">{count(b.sc.length)}</td>
          <td>Register download dated {b.registerDate}; return edition of {b.scEdition}</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href={url(AU_BASE)}>Australia</a><span class="rw-sub">ACNC register and Annual Information Statements, Wave 1b</span></th>
          <td>Total revenue of at least {b.auThreshold}</td>
          <td class="num">{count(b.au.length)}</td>
          <td>Register dataset last modified {b.acncDate}; AIS edition of {b.auEdition}</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href={url(CA_BASE)}>Canada</a><span class="rw-sub">CRA List of charities and T3010 returns, Wave 1b</span></th>
          <td>Total revenue (line 4700) of at least {b.caThreshold}</td>
          <td class="num">{count(b.ca.length)}</td>
          <td>Identification files re-published {b.craIdentDate}; T3010 edition captured {b.caEdition}</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="hubs">Browse the hubs</h2>
  <p><strong>U.S. states and territories.</strong> {count(w.stateHubs.length)} hubs by IRS mailing-address state.</p>
  <ul class="rw-hub-grid">
    {w.stateHubs.map((st) => <li><a href={url(usStatePath(st))}>{w.stateName(st)}</a> ({count(w.byState.get(st)!.length)})</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p><strong>NTEE major groups.</strong> {count(w.groupHubs.length)} hubs by the IRS classification of primary exempt activity, plus {count(w.stateGroupHubs.length)} state and group hubs.</p>
  <ul class="rw-hub-grid">
    {w.groupHubs.map((g) => <li><a href={url(w.groupPath(g))}>{w.groupLabel(g)}</a> ({count(w.byGroup.get(g)!.length)})</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p><strong>England and Wales purposes.</strong> {count(w.purposeHubs.length)} hubs by the register’s “What” classification.</p>
  <ul class="rw-hub-grid">
    {w.purposeHubs.map((c) => <li><a href={url(w.purposePath(c))}>{w.ewHubs.purposes[c].description}</a> ({count(w.byPurpose.get(c)!.length)})</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Scotland purposes.</strong> {count(b.scPurposeHubs.length)} hubs by the Scottish Charity Register’s charitable purposes.</p>
  <ul class="rw-hub-grid">
    {b.scPurposeHubs.map((p) => <li><a href={url(b.scPurposePath(p))}>{sentence(p)}</a> ({count(b.scByPurpose.get(p)!.length)})</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Australia charity subtypes.</strong> {count(b.auSubtypeHubs.length)} hubs by ACNC charity subtype.</p>
  <ul class="rw-hub-grid">
    {b.auSubtypeHubs.map((c) => <li><a href={url(b.auSubtypePath(c))}>{b.subtypeLabel(c)}</a> ({count(b.auBySubtype.get(c)!.length)})</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Canada categories and designations.</strong> {count(b.caCategoryHubs.length)} CRA category hubs and {count(b.caDesignationHubs.length)} designation hubs.</p>
  <ul class="rw-hub-grid">
    {b.caCategoryHubs.map((c) => <li><a href={url(b.caCategoryPath(c))}>{b.categoryLabel(c)} ({c})</a> ({count(b.caByCategory.get(c)!.length)})</li>)}
    {b.caDesignationHubs.map((c) => <li><a href={url(b.caDesignationPath(c))}>{b.designationLabel(c)} ({c})</a> ({count(b.caByDesignation.get(c)!.length)})</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p><strong><a href={url(CAUSE_PATH)}>Cause × Country</a>.</strong> {count(b.causes.groups.length)} label-level cause groups set the five registers’ own category labels side by side. The categories are not identical across registers, and the page is not a crosswalk.</p>

  <h2 id="files">Dataset files</h2>
  <p>The builders, <code>scripts/build-registry-wave1.py</code> and <code>scripts/build-registry-wave1b.py</code>, refuse any input whose SHA-256 fingerprint differs from the recorded one, and <code>scripts/check-registry-wave1.mjs</code> and <code>scripts/check-registry-wave1b.mjs</code> re-verify every figure against the committed editions on each build.</p>
  <p><strong>Wave 1</strong> (United States, England and Wales):</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={url(`${WAVE1_DATA_PATH}manifest.json`)} download="charitology-registry-wave1-manifest.json">manifest.json</a>: selection rules, source URLs, retrieval times and fingerprints.</li>
    {files.map((f) => <li><a href={url(`${WAVE1_DATA_PATH}${f.path}`)} download={`charitology-${f.path}`}>{f.path}</a>: {count(f.bytes)} bytes, SHA-256 <code>{f.sha256}</code>.</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Wave 1b</strong> (Scotland, Australia, Canada and Cause × Country):</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={url(`${WAVE1B_DATA_PATH}manifest.json`)} download="charitology-registry-wave1b-manifest.json">manifest.json</a>: selection rules, source URLs, retrieval times and fingerprints.</li>
    {filesB.map((f) => <li><a href={url(`${WAVE1B_DATA_PATH}${f.path}`)} download={`charitology-wave1b-${f.path}`}>{f.path}</a>: {count(f.bytes)} bytes, SHA-256 <code>{f.sha256}</code>.</li>)}
  </ul>

  <Faq faqs={faqs} />
</Entry>
